@title EHR downtime procedures
@subtitle Runbook for charge nurses and front-desk staff when the electronic health record is unavailable
@author Pelican Bay Clinic, Clinical Operations
@date 2026-11-15

kpi Declare after | 10 min | unavailable or unusably slow | neutral
kpi IT service desk | ext. 5000 | call on declaring | neutral
kpi Scan paper within | 4 h | after restoration | neutral
kpi Reconcile meds within | 24 h | after restoration | neutral

!!! The allergy list in the downtime binder is the source of truth until the record is back.

# Declare downtime
Downtime is declared when the record has been unavailable or unusably slow for 10 minutes.
- The charge nurse announces "Paper procedures" on the overhead page.
- The charge nurse calls the IT service desk on extension 5000.

# During downtime
1. Switch to paper
-- 1. Take the downtime binder from each station. It holds the printed schedule (refreshed at 05:00 daily), an allergy list and a medication list for every patient booked that day.
-- 2. Label every paper form with a patient label sheet.
2. Check in patients
-- 1. Confirm identity with two identifiers: name and date of birth.
-- 2. Record the arrival time by hand.
3. Orders and medications
-- 1. Write down every verbal order and read it back.
-- 2. Never give a high-risk medication without a second nurse's check.
-- 3. Record every dose on the paper medication sheet.
4. Keep care moving
-- 1. Do not cancel visits solely because of downtime.
-- 2. Tell patients about any delay beyond 20 minutes.

!! Never give a high-risk medication without a second nurse's check.

# Recovery
1. When IT announces restoration, wait for the all-clear before entering anything.
2. Scan paper documents into the record within 4 hours.
3. Reconcile medication entries within 24 hours.
4. Report the event on the incident form.

# Contacts
table = role,contact; IT service desk,extension 5000; Charge nurse supervisor,Rowena Achterberg; Privacy officer,Idris Mbeki
! Tell the privacy officer, Idris Mbeki, if any paper forms are lost.
